This licence covers the CODE in this repository only: the ETL pipeline, the
Astro site, the components, the scripts and the checks.

It does not cover the data or the writing, which are licensed separately:

  The four datasets coded by this project - the Governance Readiness Index,
  the AI Law and Policy Index, the Frontier Safety Framework Index and the
  Compute Threshold Index - together with the written explanations on the
  site, are licensed CC BY 4.0:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  Everything else on the site is reproduced from other people's datasets
  under their own licences and remains theirs. Those licences are not ours
  to widen. Every source, with its licence, is listed at
  https://aisafetytracker.org/sources/ and in data/sources.json.

The split is deliberate. Creative Commons themselves advise against using CC
licences for software, because they say nothing about source code, linking or
patents; MIT is the right instrument for code, and CC BY 4.0 is the right one
for data and prose.
